### v1.1.2
  - Fixed Continuous Spinning & Refresh State Bug: Eliminated over-broad `source.indexOf("apt ")` check in `main.qml` that falsely classified package count checks (`apt list`) as running upgrades, which permanently locked the widget in `isOnUpdate = true` and caused the icon animation and `↻` badge to run infinitely.
  - Refresh Spinner Icon: Replaced awkward diagonal arrow spinning animation with the standard Breeze circular refresh arrows (`view-refresh.svg`), delivering a smooth and natural loading animation during package upgrades.
  - Flexible Check Interval: Added Minute(s), Hour(s), and Day(s) unit selector (`updateIntervalUnit`) in Commands configuration, allowing check intervals ranging from minutes up to multiple days with full backward compatibility and capitalized unit labels ("Dakika", "Saat", "Gün").
  - Horizontal Scrollbar & Anti-Paging Architecture: Enabled bottom horizontal scroll bar (`horizontalScrollBarPolicy: AsNeeded`) on the Commands configuration page to allow smooth left/right scrolling to reach long command pipelines, and decoupled horizontal focus shifts in `ensureVisible` to eliminate unwanted horizontal paging/jumping effects when clicking on command inputs or Alt-Tabbing.
  - Mouse Drag Text Selection & Command Overflow Width Fix: Fixed frozen text drag selection inside command fields by restricting Flickable gestures to vertical-only (`flickableDirection = Flickable.VerticalFlick`), preventing Flickable from stealing horizontal mouse drag gestures. Bound text field preferred widths to their actual content width (`Math.max(750, contentWidth + Kirigami.Units.gridUnit * 2)`) and enabled dynamic content width scaling on the page, ensuring full visibility of extended command pipelines without clipping when scrolled horizontally to the right.
  - Centered Layout for Display, General, Popup, Notifications, and Mouse Settings: Restored clean centered alignment in `configDisplay.qml`, `configPopup.qml`, `configNotification.qml`, and `configMouse.qml`, centered the General section of `configCommand.qml`, centered headings and relative contents in Display, while preserving full-width layout for command inputs and bounded width for explanatory notes.
  - 100% Turkish Translation Coverage: Complete GNU Gettext catalog with 105 translated strings.

### v1.1.1
  - Pre-flight DPkg/APT Lock Check & Conflict Prevention: Prevents race conditions and lock aborts when `apt`, `dpkg`, or `unattended-upgrades` is already running in an external terminal (e.g. waiting at an interactive Y/n prompt). Upgrade buttons are safely disabled with informative tooltips and an inline informational banner in the popup.
  - Non-blocking Lock Timeouts: Injected `-o DPkg::Lock::Timeout=10` into all APT count, simulation, and upgrade commands to gracefully handle transient lock contention.
  - Systemd Shutdown Inhibit: Protected silent background upgrades with `systemd-inhibit --what=shutdown:sleep` to prevent power-off or suspend while packages are being unpacked/configured.
  - Infinite Retry Loop & CPU DoS Prevention: Replaced unthrottled immediate error-retry loops with a 5-second backoff timer capped at 2 attempts, eliminating CPU pegging on persistent failures.
  - Concurrency Reference Counting: Tracked concurrent background operations with `activeJobs` reference counting, ensuring the refresh spinner and active state remain visible until all asynchronous jobs complete.
  - Badge & Metric Sanitization: Enforced strict numeric regex validation on counts to prevent `NaN` badges or invalid active states.
  - Self-Healing Error Recovery: Automatically cleared sticky error state (`hasError = false`) upon subsequent successful checks.
  - Notification Aggregation: Debounced desktop alerts across multi-provider checks (500ms debounce) to eliminate duplicate/spam notifications.
  - Shell Injection Hardening: Sanitized package names in single-package upgrades against shell metacharacters.
  - Dead Code Removal: Removed obsolete `contents/_toolbox/` legacy files and unused imports.
  - 100% Turkish Translation Coverage: Full localization coverage for all new package manager lock banners and tooltips.

### v1.1.0
  - Full Left-Aligned Settings Architecture: Unified all 5 configuration tabs (`configCommand.qml`, `configNotification.qml`, `configDisplay.qml`, `configPopup.qml`, `configMouse.qml`, plus `showLog.qml`) into single, left-aligned, full-width `Kirigami.FormLayout` containers.
  - CheckBox Inline Button/Text Atomic Alignment: Replaced detached `Kirigami.FormData.label` on checkboxes with native `text:` and section grouping. Activation buttons now sit alongside their text labels, preventing them from falling underneath sentences on compact/high-DPI displays (e.g. 12.5" FHD @ 120% scale) or being pushed to the far right margin.
  - Multi-Monitor Responsive Stability: Enforced `wideMode: true` and DPI-resilient grid unit scaling across all settings tabs, eliminating spontaneous narrow-mode drops and layout jitter.
  - Cleaned Obsolete Multi-FormLayouts: Eliminated fragmented nested FormLayouts inside ColumnLayouts that caused centered floating islands in Display, Popup, and Mouse action tabs.
  - 100% Turkish Translation Coverage: Updated `.po` catalog and compiled `.mo` binary with 100 translated strings, 0 fuzzy, 0 untranslated.

### v1.0.9
  - Dedicated Notifications Settings Tab: Consolidated `configNotification.qml` grouping all notification controls (`notifyOnUpdates`, `notifyOnRebootRequired`, `notifyOnSilentUpdate`) with an explicit fail-safe policy notice
  - System Restart Desktop Notification: Automated, once-per-state-change desktop alert when `/var/run/reboot-required` is detected
  - Clean Configuration Hierarchy: Removed scattered notification checkboxes from Display and Command tabs for clean separation of concerns
  - Updated Project Governance: Refreshed `AUTHORS`, `CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md`, and practical development/testing guidelines in `CONTRIBUTING.md`
  - Refreshed Visual Assets: Updated screenshots and preview images in `git-assets/img/` reflecting Kubuntu / KDE Plasma 6
  - Complete Localization: 100% Turkish translation coverage for all new notification controls, headings, and system restart messages

### v1.0.8
  - Dynamic Provider Auto-Discovery: Automatically detect if `snap` or `flatpak` binaries exist on system (`hasSnap`, `hasFlatpak`); eliminate redundant subshells if absent
  - Graceful Settings Degradation: Disabled checkboxes with contextual `(not installed)` labels in settings when Snap or Flatpak is not installed
  - Safe Single Package Upgrades: Notify user via native desktop alert if attempting to upgrade a package whose manager is missing
  - Updated Translations: Turkish localization for all new provider status messages and configuration labels

### v1.0.7
  - Metadata Localization: Add `Description[tr]` and `Name[tr]` to `metadata.json` for native KDE Turkish About tab presentation
  - Author Credits: Refine Turkish author descriptors in `metadata.json` (`hadbilen (Ubuntu, Debian, Snap & Flatpak Portu)`, `Alan Bouteiller <a2n> (Orijinal Archupdate Geliştiricisi)`)
  - Shortcuts Tab Localization: Translate KDE Plasma shortcut label (`Activate widget as if clicked:`)
  - Popup Color Preview Localization: Localize `PackageName from source` sample text in popup settings (`configPopup.qml`)

### v1.0.6
  - Silent Background Updates: Run upgrades in the background via `pkexec` without opening a terminal window (`silentUpdate`)
  - Fail-Safe Desktop Notifications: Optional completion notification with guaranteed critical failure notifications (`notifyOnSilentUpdate`)
  - Ubuntu Phased Updates Management: Accurately exclude or forcibly include staged phased updates (`includePhasedUpdates`)
  - Rich Lifecycle Tray/Panel Icon States: Smooth rotation animation while updating, distinct negative error state (`!`), and badge indicators
  - Responsive Popup Layout: Grid-unit width constraints (320px - 580px) and right-elided package names preventing UI overflow
  - Updated Translations: Turkish localization for all new configuration toggles and lifecycle states

### v1.0.5
  - Fix terminal closing prematurely on upgrade by enforcing a `bash -c` wrapper for compound shell pipelines (`sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade`)
  - Fix `cmd` variable shadowing in `main.qml` `onExited` that caused `TypeError` and stuck refresh spinner
  - Filter out benign Qt/KDE runtime warnings from stderr in `Full.qml`
  - Keep terminal open upon failure with pause prompt so errors can be inspected
  - Reset update state properly in `Compact.qml`

### v1.0.4
  - Independent selective toggles for Snap and Flatpak updates (`enableSnapUpdates` and `enableFlatpakUpdates`)
  - Dynamic generation of count, list, and full upgrade commands according to active package managers
  - Zero-cycle resource optimization when secondary managers are disabled (APT-only mode)
  - Updated settings UI and documentation

